              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:20px 0 8px;">
                How the Hunt Works
              </h3>
              <ol style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  At the start, the fox begins transmitting.
                  Take an initial bearing from the start
                  location.
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Drive to multiple vantage points across the
                  region to take additional bearings. Plot them
                  on a map to triangulate the fox&rsquo;s
                  location.
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  When you are confident of the location,
                  drive to the area. Park, grab your HT and
                  Yagi, and complete the final leg on foot.
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Find the fox, note your time, and complete the
                  finish leg to the hidden location.
                </li>
              </ol>

              <h3 style="color:#1a3a5c;margin:20px 0 8px;">
                What to Bring
              </h3>
              <ul style="margin:8px 0;padding-left:20px;">
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Vehicle with radio mounted or handheld HT on
                  147.42&nbsp;MHz simplex
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Directional antenna for bearing-taking
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Step attenuator for the close-in on-foot leg
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Map of greater Puget Sound or a mapping app
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Comfortable walking shoes for the final leg
                </li>
                <li style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                  Water, snacks, and a full tank of fuel
                </li>
              </ul>

              <p style="background-color:#fce4e4;border-left:4px solid
                        #c62828;padding:12px 16px;margin:20px 0;
                        font-size:14px;">
                <strong>Safety reminder:</strong> Stay on public
                roads and legal pedestrian routes only, and follow
                hunt-day boundary instructions.
              </p>

              <p>
                Questions? Contact
                <strong>Tom Sayles, KE4HET</strong> at
                [TOM-EMAIL].
              </p>
              <p>
                Participation is open (no registration required). Check
                in with net control at hunt start or when you begin
                hunting. RSVP is requested, not required.
              </p>

              <p>
                See you on the hunt! 73 de KE4HET
              </p>

